[# docs-src/repos/cx-binding-python.cxd — the PyPI binding's page, served as
   repo-<this file's name>.html (RULED: DOCS-41, DOCS-47, DOCS-49 wave 4).
   Facts from the registries; the one example from the front door's ABI
   vectors, the corpus the binding grades itself against. The
   prose names no host language (DOCS-43; the letter on voice.cxd's
   bindings row stands) — the repository's own name is the one mention. #]

[repo name=cx-binding-python
  [intro
    """The same C ABI, in the host's own idiom. This binding is
       `cxlib` on PyPI: a thin wrapper over `libcx`'s string-in, string-out
       C ABI, so a program in the host language parses, canonicalises,
       hashes, converts and evaluates CX with the very engine the `cx`
       binary runs — byte-identical answers, nothing reimplemented."""]
  [body
    """Layer 1 is the contract every binding shares: sixteen canonical
       methods — parse, bytes, hash, equals, eval, select, modify and the
       node accessors — with identical semantics across hosts, so a document
       hashed here is the document hashed from anywhere else. Identity rides
       `cx_canonical`, `cx_hash` and `cx_eq`; selection, evaluation and
       update delegate to `cx_code_eval`; nothing about a document is
       retained inside `libcx` between calls. [[layer-1]] is the table,
       [[c-abi]] the surface beneath it, [[layer-2]] the host-idiomatic
       sugar above it — the idioms package — that desugars to Layer 1."""]
  [body
    """We grade the binding against the front door's published ABI vectors —
       one case per entry point a wrapper covers, an input document and the
       canonical output, hash or refusal it must answer — through the
       binding's own test, which loads the file from its pin and asserts
       every vector through its own wrapper. The same file is checked
       against `libcx` directly by the front door's C test, so the wrapper
       and the engine are held to one witness."""]
  [gives
    """No CX module: a binding ships host code, not `.cx` files, so the table
       below is the generator's note. What it gives you is the package
       itself — the Layer-1 methods, and the idioms above them that desugar
       to Layer 1."""]
  [try
    """One ABI vector, replayed by this site's `cx`: a document with a
       presentation comment, kept through `cx_fmt` — the lossless canonical
       text the wrapper's `fmt` answers. The binding's own test asserts the same
       vector through the wrapper; this page shows the engine's own answer."""]
  [fixture id=abi-001-fmt-lossless-retains-comment]
  [status
    """The binding is not consumed by `cx` — it consumes `cx`: its own
       `deps.cxd` pins the front door for the C ABI and the V core it builds
       `libcx` from, which is why the registry row carries no `at=` and the
       figure draws no column on either side. It ships from its own
       repository at its own cadence, and a pin moves there only when the
       newer front door passes with it."""]]
